@page "/terms"

<PageTitle>Terms | ksamods.gg</PageTitle>

<div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated 8 August 2026.</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">What this site is</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                ksamods.gg is an index of mods for Kitten Space Agency. We don't host mod files.
                A listing points at a file in the author's own repository, and we keep the link,
                a hash of the archive we checked, and whatever our validator learned from reading
                it. When you download a mod, you're downloading it from the author, not from us.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
                We aren't affiliated with RocketWerkz. Kitten Space Agency is their game.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Installing mods is your risk</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                Code mods are ordinary .NET assemblies. The game loads them into its own process,
                which means they can do anything your user account can do: read your files, open
                network connections, run other programs. Nothing about that is sandboxed.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
                Our validator checks that an archive is packaged the way the game expects. It
                reads the manifest, resolves the declared paths, and records what the mod ships.
                It can't tell you whether the code inside is safe. A mod passing
                validation isn't us vouching for it.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">If you publish here</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                You keep ownership of your work. By listing it you're telling us we can index it
                and show its metadata, and you're confirming you have the right to distribute it
                under the license you picked.
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-muted-foreground">
                <li>Don't publish someone else's work as your own.</li>
                <li>Don't publish anything built to damage a system or take data from it.</li>
                <li>Keep your listing honest about what the mod does.</li>
                <li>Ids are permanent. Pick one you can live with.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Moderation</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                We can delist anything that breaks the rules above. Delisting removes a mod from
                this index and stops us offering its download. It doesn't touch the author's
                repository, and it doesn't reach copies people have already installed. Ids stay
                resolvable after a delisting, so anything that pinned one doesn't silently break.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">No warranty</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                The site is provided as is. We do our best to keep it accurate and available, but
                we can't promise either, and we aren't liable for what a mod does to your game,
                your save files, or your machine. Metadata can be wrong. Links rot. Authors
                delete things.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Changes</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                If these terms change in a way that matters, we'll say so on the site rather
                than quietly editing this page. Carrying on using ksamods.gg after a change means
                you accept it.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Getting in touch</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
                Email
                <a href="mailto:contact@@ksamods.gg" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-foreground">contact@@ksamods.gg</a>
                for problems with a listing, takedown requests, or anything else. If a listing
                infringes your work, tell us what it is and what it copies, and we'll act on it
                rather than wait for a form.
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
</div>
